# ============================================================================
# tiny-talk: say it in pictures anyone can read.
#
#   A messenger. Type in your own language: what travels is only pictures, and
#   it arrives in the reader's language. Each message shows both, so using it
#   is learning it. Link two phones (or a phone and a browser) by showing a
#   code, scanning one, or pressing together; nobody in between can read it.
#   📖 looks up any word in 19 languages; 🎓 has lessons with a quiz.
#   Every message and word is shown in Blissymbols too (BCI's own drawings),
#   so anyone who knows Bliss can read along, and learners pick it up.
#
#   The pictures write the words of Blissymbolics, a language of meanings
#   rather than sounds, built from a few hundred basic characters. Each basic
#   character has one emoji, so every word follows from Bliss's own recipe:
#   teacher = person + giving + knowledge = 🧑🎁🎓.
#
#   Bliss words, recipes and their 19 languages: BCI Authorized Vocabulary
#   2026-09-12, CC BY-SA 4.0, Blissymbolics Communication International
#   (blissymbolics.org). The dictionary in this app shares that licence:
#   github.com/wallisoft/tiny-talk. The app's own code: MIT.
#
#   Made with Visualised.
# ============================================================================

@Window TinyTalk
Title=tiny-talk
Version=0.7.1
Width=360
Height=652
WebAddress=https://tiny-talk.world/chat.html
AppBar=true
Terms=https://tiny-talk.world/terms.html
About=Say it in pictures anyone can read. Blissymbols and their words: Blissymbolics Communication International, CC BY-SA 4.0. The app's code: MIT, by Wallisoft.
UpdateFrom=https://visualised.org/downloads/TinyTalk.vml
UpdateApk=https://visualised.org/downloads/TinyTalk.apk
OnOpened=Opened
AndroidPackage=io.visualised.made.tinytalk.k7b1ce6cd
AndroidKey=7b1ce6cd

@Canvas c
Parent=TinyTalk
Background=#F4F1FB

# --- the header: an indigo band with the tabs as pills (the one showing is white) ---
